["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ecli", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[European Case Law Identifier (ECLI)](https://data.europa.eu/data/datasets/european-case-law-identifier-ecli) is a uniform identifier for judicial decisions across Europe. It consists of five mandatory components: the \"ECLI\" prefix, a country code, a court code, the year of the decision, and a unique serial number (e.g., `ECLI:EU:C:2023:94`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/hsCodes", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The [Harmonized System (HS)](https://www.wcoomd.org/en/topics/nomenclature/overview/what-is-the-harmonized-system.aspx) of tariff nomenclature is an internationally standardized system of names and numbers, defined by the World Customs Organization, used to classify traded products.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
